{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9wsdW269KW7VaQCPmkL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've fixed it: patterns passed with `--and` now get the same path-separator error as the main pattern. Before, a command like `fd foo --and a/b` ran and returned nothing; now it stops with the error and suggests the `fd . 'a/b'` and `fd --full-path 'a/b'` alternatives. The full test suite passes, including two new tests. Nothing is committed yet.\n\n**Change (`src/main.rs`)**\n- `ensure_search_pattern_is_not_a_path` now checks the main pattern and then each `--and` pattern, and reports the first one that contains a separator. `--full-path` still turns the check off for all of them.\n- The check for a single pattern is now its own small function, `pattern_looks_like_a_path`. The rules are unchanged: `/` always triggers the error, and on Windows `\\` triggers it only when the pattern is an existing directory.\n\n**Tests (`tests/tests.rs`)**\n- `test_and_pattern_with_forward_slash_is_rejected`: an `--and` pattern containing `/` gives the error, both for a real directory (`one/two`) and for a path that doesn't exist (`nonexistent/path`).\n- `test_and_pattern_with_forward_slash_allowed_with_full_path`: with `--full-path`, `foo --and one/two` returns its matches instead of erroring.\n\nI also added a line under Unreleased → Bugfixes in `CHANGELOG.md`.\n\nClippy shows warnings in `tests/tests.rs`, but they're on lines this change doesn't touch."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":366,"cache_read_input_tokens":38234,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":366,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":514,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"214272f0-7033-47a3-8188-74364da79fab","uuid":"d15444a3-32c6-4ee1-b8e1-85b82f107b03","timestamp":"2026-10-18T15:34:18.987Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9wsdGsTR7mMeWbpg2Wd"}
