- `ensure_search_pattern_is_not_a_path` now checks the main pattern and then each `--and` pattern, and reports the first one that contains a separator. `--full-path` still turns the check off for all of them.\n- The check for a single pattern is now its own small function, `pattern_looks_like_a_path`. The rules are unchanged: `/` always triggers the error, and on Windows `\\` triggers it only when the pattern is an existing directory.\n\n**Tests (`tests/tests.rs`)**\n- `test_and_pattern_with_forward_slash_is_rejected`: an `--and` pattern containing `/` gives the error, both for a real directory (`one/two`) and for a path that doesn't exist (`nonexistent/path`).\n- `test_and_pattern_with_forward_slash_allowed_with_full_path`: with `--full-path`, `foo --and one/two` returns its matches instead of erroring.\n\nI also added a line under Unreleased → Bugfixes in `CHANGELOG.md`.\n\nClippy shows warnings in `tests/tests.rs`, but they're on lines this change doesn't touch.","ttft_ms":2528,"type":"result","duration_ms":108586,"uuid":"82ca6212-4794-43ce-b0cf-2c293620db21","ttft_stream_ms":1032,"time_to_request_ms":209,"first_content_frame_ms":1033,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
